WEBVTT

00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:14.026
Hi, friends. Gani here. This is The Strategy Matchmaker.

00:00:14.026 --> 00:00:20.052
Sit tall in your chair. Feet flat on the floor.

00:00:20.052 --> 00:00:23.668
Hands resting on your desk. Shoulders soft.

00:00:23.668 --> 00:00:27.283
Take one slow breath with me… and let it go.

00:00:27.283 --> 00:00:35.719
You already own a whole shelf of strategies. Breathing. Naming. Moving. Resting. Asking. Space.

00:00:35.719 --> 00:00:45.361
Here is the part nobody says out loud: a strategy works best when it fits the feeling that showed up.

00:00:45.361 --> 00:00:56.208
A strategy that does not fit is not broken, and neither are you. It is just the wrong match for this feeling, this time.

00:00:56.208 --> 00:01:01.029
Matching is a skill, and like every skill, it is learned by trying. Let me show you how matching works.

00:01:01.029 --> 00:01:11.875
Big energy in the body — wiggly, buzzy, too-much-inside energy — often fits movement. Shake it out. Stretch tall. Let the body spend what it is holding.

00:01:11.875 --> 00:01:22.722
A wobbly worry — a thought that keeps circling — often fits naming it. Say the worry plainly, to yourself or a grown-up. Named worries get smaller edges.

00:01:22.722 --> 00:01:33.569
Tangled anger often fits space first, and words after. Room to cool, then the talking. Words land better when the body has settled.

00:01:33.569 --> 00:01:43.210
A heavy, droopy feeling often fits rest or a cozy corner. Not every feeling needs fixing. Some need quiet company.

00:01:43.210 --> 00:01:44.416
Four feelings, four different fits. The feeling is the clue. The strategy is the match.

00:01:44.416 --> 00:01:55.262
Now the most important part: if you try a strategy and it does not fit, you have not failed anything.

00:01:55.262 --> 00:02:06.109
Switching strategies IS the skill. Trying a second match means the matchmaker in you is working.

00:02:06.109 --> 00:02:14.545
There is no single right answer here, and nobody is grading your matches. A match that worked yesterday might not fit today. That is allowed.

00:02:14.545 --> 00:02:15.751
Feelings are never ranked — not good ones and bad ones, just feelings. Each one is a clue, and each clue points to a fit.

00:02:15.751 --> 00:02:24.187
Name the feeling. Try a match. Switch if it doesn't fit.

00:02:24.187 --> 00:02:30.213
Shoulders soft. Let your body rest.

00:02:30.213 --> 00:02:35.034
Hands down. One more slow breath… and let it go.

00:02:35.034 --> 00:02:41.060
Eyes open. Look around your classroom.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:47.086
You're ready for what's next.
